Sure! If you feed those coordinates into the Google Maps Geocoding API (using a request like `https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY`), the API will return a JSON payload that includes the formatted address and other metadata.

Here’s what you’d typically see in the response:

```json
